WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.036
That service, that commitment,
honor, pride.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.571
That's why I became
a police officer.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.109
My name is Michael Dominique.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.011
I serve in the United States
Marine Corps.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.412
I left as a sergeant.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.781
I served in Iraq
and South America.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.684
I'm here as a police officer
at Yale University.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.886
One of the hardest things
coming back from Iraq

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:23.890
was acclimating back
into everyday society.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.026
People don't know exactly
what you’ve gone through,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.627
especially if you've
gone to war.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:31.364
They don't know that camaraderie
that you've had

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.100
when you've served alongside
other veterans.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.635
The majority of the
service members

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.438
that I looked up to growing up,
they're no longer here.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.608
Before a lot of them passed,
I was able to show

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.644
that sign of respect
by becoming a marine,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.212
joining the service.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.416
So, that’s what
Veterans Day means to me.

